<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guadalajara (Mexico)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guadalajara is the capital of the Mexican state of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jalisco">Jalisco</a> and one of the largest cities in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>. Founded by Spanish settlers in 1532 and moved to its present site in the Atemajac valley in 1542, it became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/audiencia">Audiencia</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-galicia">New Galicia</a> and the main centre of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viceroyalty-of-new-spain">New Spain</a>. Mariachi music and tequila both come from the surrounding region.</p></div>
